1
00:00:00,397 --> 00:00:01,456
R T Safe.

2
00:00:04,381 --> 00:00:06,482
The world does not pause while an agent thinks.

3
00:00:07,089 --> 00:00:09,712
Static evaluation freezes the world during inference.

4
00:00:10,322 --> 00:00:12,549
In real time, pedestrians keep moving, and a

5
00:00:12,559 --> 00:00:14,039
clear path can become unsafe.

6
00:00:15,397 --> 00:00:18,767
Navigate to the goal across five maps and thirty-six routes.

7
00:00:19,510 --> 00:00:24,861
Safety includes collisions, trip, oil and water hazards, and traffic-rule violations.

8
00:00:27,397 --> 00:00:29,352
How do frontier agents perform?

9
00:00:30,083 --> 00:00:32,750
On the same recorded route, Astra makes twelve

10
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:34,338
decisions with one collision.

11
00:00:35,083 --> 00:00:38,205
Sol makes thirty-three decisions with seventeen collisions.

12
00:00:38,939 --> 00:00:41,873
Recorded behavior, reconstructed in NYC.

13
00:00:43,397 --> 00:00:46,638
Sonnet records the fewest collisions; Grok, the most.

14
00:00:47,368 --> 00:00:49,182
Inkling favors longer moves.

15
00:00:49,916 --> 00:00:51,611
Sol turns and waits most.

16
00:00:52,345 --> 00:00:55,326
Response time and action choices both shape behavior.

17
00:00:57,379 --> 00:00:58,781
Task completion is not enough.

18
00:00:59,369 --> 00:01:01,993
Success reaches ninety-four point four percent, but safe

19
00:01:02,003 --> 00:01:04,057
success is only zero point seven percent.

20
00:01:05,392 --> 00:01:09,430
On matched hard routes, real-time collisions rise twelve point three times.

21
00:01:10,125 --> 00:01:12,941
About eighty-four percent occur while the agent is deciding.

22
00:01:14,397 --> 00:01:16,564
More reasoning is not reliably safer.

23
00:01:17,307 --> 00:01:20,068
From default to higher effort, collisions rise from

24
00:01:20,078 --> 00:01:22,588
forty point seven to sixty-two per episode.

25
00:01:24,391 --> 00:01:26,637
R T Safe supports reinforcement learning.

26
00:01:27,325 --> 00:01:28,956
Reward design shapes safety.
